sharp-libvips (LGPL-3.0-or-later) — transitive, JS dependency tree
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`sharp`, an image-processing library present in this project's JavaScript
dependency tree (`bun.lock`), bundles prebuilt native binaries of
`libvips` via the optional `@img/sharp-libvips-*` packages. `libvips` itself
is distributed under LGPL-3.0-or-later.

- `sharp`'s own JavaScript bindings are Apache-2.0.
- The `@img/sharp-libvips-*` binaries are LGPL-3.0-or-later, dynamically
  linked (not statically compiled into this project's own code).
- LGPL-3.0 permits dynamic linking from a project under a different license
  (including Apache-2.0) without imposing the LGPL on the linking project's
  own source, provided the LGPL-covered component itself remains replaceable
  and its license/source-availability obligations are respected.
- Upstream source for `libvips` is available at
  https://github.com/libvips/libvips and for the `sharp-libvips` packaging at
  https://github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips.

This dependency was surfaced in a license audit prior to open-sourcing this
repository and is called out here for transparency; it does not affect the
license of this project's own source code (Apache-2.0).

